  "description": "<p>This bug can be seen when attempting to create a BasicContainer with an RDF body, but without a provided content-type. The bug is that the body of the HTTP response to the client is an internal stacktrace. The fix should catch the exception, include a simple error message (e.g. \"Content-Type header required\"), and a 400 response code.</p>\n\n<p>To recreate this bug:<br/>\n$ curl -i -d \"&lt;&gt; &lt;<a href=\"http://awoods.com#title\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://awoods.com#title</a>&gt; 'A title'\" -XPUT localhost:8080/rest/test -H'Link: &lt;<a href=\"http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://www.w3.org/ns/ldp#BasicContainer</a>&gt;;rel=\"type\"'</p>",
